      "writtenOn": "2026-07-17T08:50:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we reject chains containing a zero-length segment during the pre-scan? VPP only asserts that the head is non-empty; empty continuation buffers can exist. AF_XDP treats a zero-length descriptor as invalid and does not produce completions for that packet, so these buffers would leak and repeated packets could exhaust the pool.",
      "revId": "46a5463547885367bd8c2506ca40fd34e0562184",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
